---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout basePath="" title="Symptoms of a Loop | Ask Astro Raja">
  <!-- PAGE HEADER -->
  <section class="pt-32 pb-16 px-4 bg-brand-light-bg text-center border-b border-brand-border">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-brand-saffron font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-6 text-sm md:text-base">
        Clinical Observation
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy mb-6 tracking-tight">Symptoms of a Loop.</h1>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-brand-text leading-relaxed font-medium max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        A behavioral pattern does not announce itself. It disguises itself as your personality, your circumstances, and your "bad luck." 
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTENT -->
  <section class="py-24 px-4 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-16">
      
      <!-- Symptom 1 -->
      <div class="bg-white border border-brand-border rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm flex flex-col md:flex-row">
        <div class="bg-brand-navy p-8 md:w-1/3 flex flex-col justify-center text-white">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-brand-saffron tracking-widest uppercase mb-2">Subject A</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">The Chronic Giver</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Identified pattern: Worth = Utility</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8 md:w-2/3">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-4">The Invisible Symptom:</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Subject A is exhausted. They are the person everyone calls when there is a crisis. They pride themselves on being deeply empathetic and supportive. However, they are secretly deeply resentful. They feel entirely unsupported by their friends and partners. 
          </p>
          <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-6">
            <strong>The Loop:</strong> They actively subconsciously select partners and friends who are in crisis, because their behavioral blueprint dictates that if they are not "useful," they will be abandoned. They construct a prison of dependents, and then complain about being trapped.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 border-l-4 border-brand-saffron rounded-r-lg text-sm font-medium text-brand-navy">
            "I just have bad luck with finding people who can take care of me."
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Symptom 2 -->
      <div class="bg-white border border-brand-border rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm flex flex-col md:flex-row">
        <div class="bg-brand-navy p-8 md:w-1/3 flex flex-col justify-center text-white">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-brand-saffron tracking-widest uppercase mb-2">Subject B</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">The Paralysis Engineer</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Identified pattern: Perfection as Shield</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8 md:w-2/3">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-4">The Invisible Symptom:</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Subject B is incredibly intelligent. They have three brilliant business ideas and have spent the last 18 months "researching." They read every book on productivity. They optimize their morning routine. Yet, they haven't launched a single thing.
          </p>
          <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-6">
            <strong>The Loop:</strong> They use "preparation" as a sophisticated mechanism to avoid failure. Their blueprint equates failure with a total loss of identity. Therefore, as long as they are "preparing," they never have to face the market. They are trapped in the illusion of motion while remaining completely stationary.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 border-l-4 border-brand-saffron rounded-r-lg text-sm font-medium text-brand-navy">
            "I'm almost ready to launch. I just need to figure out this one last detail."
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Symptom 3 -->
      <div class="bg-white border border-brand-border rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm flex flex-col md:flex-row">
        <div class="bg-brand-navy p-8 md:w-1/3 flex flex-col justify-center text-white">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-brand-saffron tracking-widest uppercase mb-2">Subject C</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">The Chaos Addict</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Identified pattern: Peace = Danger</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8 md:w-2/3">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-4">The Invisible Symptom:</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Subject C finally gets everything they said they wanted. A loving, stable partner. A secure job. A quiet weekend. And they are absolutely miserable. Without realizing it, they pick a fight with their partner, or they take on a wildly risky side-project that threatens their job.
          </p>
          <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-6">
            <strong>The Loop:</strong> Their early conditioning linked high stress with "normalcy." When things are peaceful, their nervous system registers it as the calm before the storm—which is terrifying. To regain control, they subconsciously detonate their own lives so they can go back to managing a crisis.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 border-l-4 border-brand-saffron rounded-r-lg text-sm font-medium text-brand-navy">
            "I don't know why I did that. I just got bored, I guess."
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="text-center mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-brand-border">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">Do you recognize your symptoms?</h3>
        <p class="text-brand-text mb-8 max-w-xl mx-auto">
          Reading about a pattern is not the same as diagnosing your own. You cannot out-think an algorithm you can't see. 
        </p>
        <a href="/get-reading" class="inline-block px-8 py-4 bg-brand-saffron text-white rounded-xl font-bold text-lg hover:scale-105 transition-transform shadow-md">
          Diagnose My Pattern
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
